v0.3.0
 - [Changed] Arrow interop uses arrow.RecordBatch (DataFrame.ToArrowRecord and NewBaseDataFrameFromArrowRecord); arrow.Record was deprecated upstream
 - [BugFix] Aggregations: grouped std used the average group size as divisor; ungrouped mean/std under removeNAs divided by the total length instead of the non-null count
 - [Changed] Evaluated Arrow-native column storage (three-regime benchmark) and decided against it; Arrow stays an interop layer (Parquet, IPC, ecosystem handoff). See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-08-arrow-native-storage-migration.md
 - [Removed] Measurement-only Arrow-native storage prototype and the unwired Arrow compute-dispatch layer (series/arrow_ops.go); neither was reachable outside its own tests. Arrow interop (Series.ArrowArray / ArrowArrayToSeries) is unchanged

v0.2.0: third-fish
 - [Changed] Library renamed from aargh to enchanter: module is now github.com/caerbannogwhite/enchanter, root package is `enchanter`
 - [Feature] Apache Arrow interop: Series.ArrowArray(), DataFrame.ArrowSchema() / ToArrowRecord(), NewBaseDataFrameFromArrowRecord()
 - [Feature] Parquet reader and writer: DataFrame.FromParquet() / ToParquet()
 - [Feature] Arrow IPC (Feather) reader and writer: DataFrame.FromArrowIPC() / ToArrowIPC()
 - [Improved] Aggregators improved, dataframe integration tests added
 - [Improved] Arrow memory: internal Arrow references are released deterministically (CheckedAllocator-clean)
 - [BugFix] Join: fixed right-dataframe column lookup
 - [BugFix] GroupBy: null group keys stay null in the result; grouping by Time/Duration keys no longer corrupts the frame; GroupBy on a grouped dataframe now regroups instead of being ignored
 - [BugFix] Parquet / Arrow IPC readers: null masks are preserved across multiple row groups / record batches
 - [BugFix] Series mutated after an Arrow conversion (Sort, Set) no longer serve stale Arrow data
 - [BugFix] Library code no longer prints debug output to stdout (constructor warnings go to stderr)
 - [Improved] Added examples
 - [WIP] SAS7BDAT reader: header and page parsing only; data reading deferred to a future release

v0.1.2: second-fish
 - [Enanchment] Added support for time in the type guesser
 - [BugFix] Type guesser boolean regex fixed
 - [BugFix] Getting the correct series type in CSV reader

v0.1.1: morning
 - [BugFix] Corrected issue where IoData was not set in DataFrame IOs
 - [BugFix] Fixed reading of XPT V8 and V9 labels
 - [BugFix] Improved parsing of XPT dates in V5 and V6
 - [BugFix] Fixed XPT version guessing logic

v0.1.0: first-fish
 - Initial release
